.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_CREATE 3 2026-08-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_create \- create a seekable MPQ archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_create("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s **" "archive,"
.BI "        const char     *" "path,"
.BI "        const mpq_archive_create_options_s *" "options"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Optional version-100 attributes work in both MPQ v1 and v2. Combine
LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_CRC32,
LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_FILETIME,
LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_MD5, and
LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_PATCH_BIT in options.attributes to select arrays.
Zero disables generation. Any nonzero combination creates one (attributes)
file and consumes one reserved slot. Unknown attribute bits are rejected.
Capacity includes the attributes entry
and listfile if enabled; the internal attributes name is reserved.
Finalization writes the listfile, attributes, then the completed tables.
Checksums cover source bytes before compression; FILETIME defaults to zero
and patch bits are zero. Use libmpq__writer_timestamp() on an active writer
for an explicit timestamp. Path addition never imports filesystem timestamps.
.PP
Creates a v1 or v2 archive at \fIpath\fP. The archive is finalized by
libmpq__archive_close(3). The options select a fixed entry capacity, sector
size, archive version, and optional generated (listfile).
.PP
Compression defaults to STANDARD. Add
LIBMPQ_ARCHIVE_CREATE_COMPRESSION_EXTENDED to options.flags to select
EXTENDED. The policy affects writer validation only, not decoding.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__archive_attributes (3),
.BR libmpq__file_attributes (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_timestamp (3),
